I heard a talk last week by this guy.  He claims to have built a
bench-top version which works over a few kilometers, and he thinks his
method could be extended up to about 10 kilometers.  (The 10K limit is
a fundamental physical limit to transmission of reasonable wavelength
photons over fiber optic cable.  You can't use amplifiers or
repeaters, since they would interfere with the quantum effects.)  

You get to figure out why you want secure delivery of keys (or other
shared random bits) over short distances.

